    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d824">

                <pb facs="0822" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg564"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1703a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        London</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 8, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department informed that in cases of seizure since blockade order in council,
                    prize court proceedings are based both on violation of blockade and on suspected
                    contraband character of goods. Investigate and report any cases in which both
                    grounds of seizure are stated in same writ.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
